A||||6||85seNUT||Borla exuast or ocelot?||||1||
Z||000000||85seNUT||02-10-2001||02:13 PM||||I already know which on is better but i am a 17 year old teenager with only some money, not lots.  I want to hear from people that have each.  Borla and ocelot,  how much did each raise your horsepower.  Sound of your engine.  Pretty much overall  performance.  thanks.  oh yea and how much did it cost you to buy it and have it installed.  or do u recomend putting it in myself?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||02-10-2001||03:28 PM||||Would be very hard to find a Borla but that's the one to go for if available. Recently was just a little over the Ocelot's $$. If you cant's find it do a search here for many other posibilities. You can install it but I recommend a muffler shop better.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TwisT||02-10-2001||10:04 PM||||Here's my suggestion,  all be it a little different...<P>NEITHER!<P>Seriously,  if your cash flow is a hurtin',  try to avoid the thought of purchasing a completely new system entirely.  Even the Ocelot (which I have on my '88 GT...  bought it that way) is plenty of money.  There is an alternative...<P>Keep your cat cuz yer in CA...  REMOVE the muffler,  substitute a straight pipe.  You are done!  Sounds great,  and is smog legal.  If they haven't changed the rules on the west coast,  you'll be fine.  If they are picky about sound levels,  I would HIGHLY recommend installing a 2-chamber Flowmaster for the best sound.  I believe a late model Camaro/Firebird version will work.<P>You don't need to buy a whole new system to get power and sound out of your Fiero.  Pontiac built one of the best factory exhaust systems ever made in our beloved Fieros.  It's been tested and proved.  <P>Good luck!<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||02-10-2001||10:04 PM||||I have Borla's on both my Fieros.  They work great, sound good.  But if you don't have the money for quality go to Midas, they will sell you a system at half the cost of a Borla, that will last a year, then if you still have the Fiero, you can replace it year after year. Free muffler, but the cost of the pipes will get you.<P>The Borlas including tips were under $1G for the pair, and I had a muffler shop do the install for $75, including replacing the cat (I supplied).<P>For Borla see Fiero Parts and Appraisals in he vendor list.||||reg||3
Z||000004||85seNUT||02-11-2001||12:32 AM||||Does anyone have a model number or a year and brand cuz i keep asking these guys and they keep telling me nothing will fit because of the tiny space that they put the muffler in.  They say nothing performance will fit because the muffler that is on there is small and all the flows and what not are bigger and will not fit.  Please if you have a model number or a brand can you please post it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||02-11-2001||02:00 AM||||Spintech 331SC (2.5" in dual 2" out) or 333SC 2.5" all around. 1" wider than stock. 13"x9"x4". Stock is 11.5" to the sides, but 12" to the climped ends. Spintechs are welded ends to I'll have to shift the left bracket over about a inch. <P>They recommended the dual 2" out to keep it quieter. They ain't light.<P>Hopefully I'll have it in in about a week. We got lots-o-snow right now.<P>Ain't cheap. $140US out the door in California.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick's Dad||02-11-2001||01:26 PM||||Although I'm going the other way (Hey, I like my neighbors now), I also recommend replacing the muggler with straight pipe.<P>Although I don't necessarily agree that we have the best stock exhaust available (The manifolds are pretty restrictive), I did notice some top end benefit (Not huge) from a new, larger Cat and straight pipes from IRM. Of course, this gain may have been the "glow" from having put something new and louder on the car, but total cost, about $450, with shipping, included the cat, 2½" OD pipes, and a pair of Hooker dual resonator tips. About $75 to install at local shop.<P>Warning about the Hookers, though. It didn't take long for them to rot and fall off. They sounded great when on, especiall once they heated up. Nice and mellow, but not quiet. I often wondered, sometimes very loudly, whith the windows down about the inattention of other drivers, i.e. "How can you not have noticed a car this loud?"<P>As I said, I'm going the other way, looking at Borla, Flowmaster, and others. My in-laws are downstairs (My father in law's bedroom is right next to the driveway), and I like the neighbors that I have, except for my next door neighbor's dog. I thought that the big ones were quiet....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/StarHeroSig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
